# Hourly verified SQLite snapshot to /Volumes/local, a disk attached to this
# Mac, then a copy of the hourly root to the NAS (sd:4009). It is the same verb
# as the nightly `sd-db-backup`; the NAS copy makes the hour also what a lost
# Mac costs, and it is what a satellite promoted to hub restores from.
#
# `--require-mount /Volumes/local` is asked before anything is written: with
# the disk detached, /Volumes/local is an ordinary directory on the boot disk,
# and a snapshot written there restores and compares perfectly on the disk it
# was meant to leave. The refusal exits 1 and mails through sd-db, so a
# detached drive is reported every hour until it is reattached.
#
# Retention is by count (sd:3637): `--keep 24` keeps the newest 24 verified
# owned snapshots, a day when every hourly run happens and longer when the
# Mac sleeps. The NAS keeps 7 days by checkpoint age, below. Only directories
# the backup wrote and still verifies are deleted; nothing else in
# "Backup Local" is touched.
#
# `--no-row-prune`: the row prune files one report item per run, which is
# right once a night and 24 items a day here. The nightly job keeps it.
#
# :50 keeps clear of the nightly job at 02:10 and of the mirror passes that
# write to this disk at 03:30, 04:30 and 16:30. The two backups write to
# different roots, and cron-jobs.sh's lock stops an hourly run overlapping
# the one before it.
#
# The NAS copy runs only if the snapshot succeeded, so it never reads a
# half-written snapshot directory, and only after offsite-verify's preflight
# shows the NAS folder is on the expected share. It is additive, with its own
# pair list, `mirrors-nas-hourly.conf` (local-mirror-sync has the example).
# The NAS folder is a placeholder: set SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER below
# and the pair list's destination to the same path, the `sd-backups-hourly`
# folder under offsite-verify's OFFSITE_VERIFY_ROOT. offsite-verify fails
# when the newest copy there is more than 3 hours old.
#
# After the copy, `sd-db backup --prune-only` deletes NAS copies whose
# checkpoint is more than 7 days old (sd:4011). It takes no snapshot, and it
# deletes only a copy whose files still match its manifest's hashes and whose
# database still verifies; a partial or foreign directory stays. It reads the
# share, so it runs under lib/bounded.sh's st_step at 300 s: a slow share once
# held it until JOB_TIMEOUT, and the log did not name the step (sd:4690). At
# the bound the step exits 124 and the job log names it; the snapshot and the
# copy before it are done.
#
# SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_DESTINATION moves the local root, as a promoted
# satellite does (sd:4009 design, "Bulk storage and paths"); an operator who
# names the destination has answered the mount question, so the check stands
# aside, as it does for the nightly job. The NAS copy still runs: set the pair
# list's source to the same root. A source the pair list names but this
# machine lacks fails the copy, and the job mails. An empty
# SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER takes the snapshot only, for a test or a
# one-off.
JOB_SCHEDULE="50 * * * *"
# Inside the hour, so a hung backup or copy frees its lock before the next slot.
JOB_TIMEOUT="20m"
SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_MOUNT=""
[ -n "${SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_DESTINATION:-}" ] || SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_MOUNT=" --require-mount /Volumes/local"
SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_SNAPSHOT="\"$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-ai-command-pack/bin/sd-db\" backup --destination \"${SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_DESTINATION:-/Volumes/local/Backup Local/sd-backups}\"$SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_MOUNT --keep 24 --no-row-prune"
SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER="${SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER-/Volumes/change-me-nas-share/Backup/sd-backups-hourly}"
SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS="\"\${SD_DB_PYTHON:-python3}\" \"$ROOT/../local-mirror-sync/offsite-verify.py\" --preflight-only --destination \"$SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER\" && MIRROR_SYNC_CONF=mirrors-nas-hourly.conf MIRROR_SYNC_ADDITIVE=1 sh \"$ROOT/../local-mirror-sync/mirror-sync.sh\" sync && . \"$ROOT/../lib/bounded.sh\" && st_step 300 \"$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-ai-command-pack/bin/sd-db\" backup --prune-only --destination \"$SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER\" --keep-days 7"
JOB_COMMAND="$SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_SNAPSHOT && $SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS"
[ -n "$SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER" ] || JOB_COMMAND="$SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_SNAPSHOT"
unset SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_MOUNT SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_SNAPSHOT SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS SD_DB_BACKUP_HOURLY_NAS_FOLDER
